#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:6
#: 7fbc3ada4ae548beb22b54d182e7588a
msgid "Transmitter Based Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:8
#: 2cd95ce4382244e4a8ec2fc07a70a5f9
msgid "You can perform extensive parameter tuning in flight using your R/C transmitter. This is meant for advanced users who are unable to use the Autotune features or wish to do fine tuning with full manual tuning control of each parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:15
#: 0a0b4860e2b14620b1ed2ac06e6f80d4
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:17
#: fbd84310d9aa4482b09439333fd1e5ef
msgid "Transmitter based tuning allows you to tune a single parameter or a set of parameters while flying. The basic idea is to link the tuning value of a parameter to a knob or slider on your transmitter then to adjust the parameter in flight by moving the knob."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:24
#: 80e6ef8dc5ce4876bd6105e1fbd1f79d
msgid "Key features of transmitter based tuning are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:26
#: 87252dc6129143b0b6185192ba9cae5d
msgid "Tune either a single parameter or a whole set of related parameters in a single flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:29
#: 036675261ac342a9b1118b14ebfac17d
msgid "Re-scale the range of the parameter value linked to the tuning knob using a \"selector switch\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:32
#: 9290fb660c814ac0a8d83e82bd6e2dcc
msgid "Switch between parameters to tune while flying using a selector switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:35
#: 87fcbd6b19ed477fbb9e0c2a326ea707
msgid "Save the new parameters in flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:37
#: 8ec88b44abd64c04b4a219d47cfe0c18
msgid "Receive audible feedback from the flight board buzzer and the GCS on tuning progress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:42
#: 81c800a59452497fba566dda515f3147
msgid "Concepts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:44
#: 729b86e1717d46d4b6b11b48b7ed8476
msgid "The two key controls for transmitter based tuning are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:46
#: a107a17bd941478bb88dd5fe318fbccb
msgid "A \"tuning knob\", setup on your transmitter to a convenient knob or slider and linked to an RC channel that your board receives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:49
#: 9ea8405ee1bf43e7b37240f4f83c96b9
msgid "An optional \"selector switch\" for controlling advanced features of the tune. This should be linked to a two position switch mapped to a RC channel that your board receives. A spring loaded switch (such as the trainer switch) works particularly well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:54
#: 8686d58531cd457b82fdae2d9ae155ad
msgid "In addition to those input controls the following concepts are useful in understanding the tuning process:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:57
#: 7ab4c5dfd1ec4f52809219d162dc0c5d
msgid "A \"parameter set\" is a group of related parameters that can be tuned one after the other in a single flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:60
#: b320ee5e812f47db97e37044336c237f
msgid "The \"mid-point\" is point on the tuning knobs range where it produces a PWM value half way between minimum and maximum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:65
#: fc907b3ce716499dbdb3b200b49333fe
msgid "Setting up for tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:67
#: ff8086e181ff4d24aaa0d3ee8c2e492f
msgid "To setup your vehicle for tuning you need to set the following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:70
#: 52b1788fdf15430aa94ac2ce4da35221
msgid ":ref:`TUNE_CHAN<TUNE_CHAN>`: the RC input channel associated with your chosen tuning knob"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:72
#: ae32fa3069374899b3ad363506064f24
msgid ":ref:`TUNE_CHAN_MIN<TUNE_CHAN_MIN>`: the minimum PWM values produced on :ref:`TUNE_CHAN<TUNE_CHAN>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:73
#: c47913f5ac034a34af5cf2e861e70f75
msgid ":ref:`TUNE_CHAN_MAX<TUNE_CHAN_MAX>`: the maximum PWM values produced on :ref:`TUNE_CHAN<TUNE_CHAN>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:74
#: 14e5d860c8fe4dca894ead880d8124c0
msgid ":ref:`TUNE_PARAM<TUNE_PARAM>`: the parameter or set of parameters you will be tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:75
#: 7fe68ce9932a4b53a74190cdbb7ef4df
msgid ":ref:`TUNE_SELECTOR<TUNE_SELECTOR>`: the RC input channel associated with your chosen selector switch (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:77
#: 2ec5ff6962504fbea39b520acf8974c2
msgid ":ref:`TUNE_RANGE<TUNE_RANGE>`: the scaling range which the tuning knob covers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:79
#: 25916124f6614671b19a9f4dd3e26085
msgid "The :ref:`TUNE_PARAM<TUNE_PARAM>` parameter selects the parameter or set of parameters you will be tuning. Values of :ref:`TUNE_PARAM<TUNE_PARAM>` less than 100 correspond to individual tunable parameters whereas values of 101 or higher correspond to sets of related parameters that can be tuned one after the other in a flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:85
#: 0c8bc737f50c43b69de0e400f1ec96ec
msgid "Most of the tuneable parameters apply to the VTOL operation of QuadPlanes. Only :ref:`TUNE_PARAM<TUNE_PARAM>` values in the 50-57 and 111-113 range are for fixed wing operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:87
#: 8791c9d3539b4e1fa71b07b5bcd81dfd
msgid "Use your ground stations parameter interface to see see the full list of tunable parameters and parameter sets available for :ref:`TUNE_PARAM<TUNE_PARAM>`. For Plane most of the parameters are associated with tuning the QuadPlane VTOL motors as those are the most difficult to tune. You can also tune some fixed wing parameters, although most people find the automatic tuning with AUTOTUNE mode is the best option for fixed wing flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:95
#: 8e25660091f745089cf233026772cea4
msgid "If you want to tune a set of parameters (by choosing a :ref:`TUNE_PARAM<TUNE_PARAM>` value over 100) you must have a selector switch configured with the :ref:`TUNE_SELECTOR<TUNE_SELECTOR>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:100
#: 2eb9357328d344b49703af73fb03fe65
msgid "Using the tuning knob"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:102
#: 5741fcffae47441d8544ccc48553be79
msgid "The basic operation of the tuning knob is very simple. If the tuning knob is at the bottom of its range then the parameter being tuned is set to the initial value divided by the :ref:`TUNE_RANGE<TUNE_RANGE>`. If the tuning knob is at the top of its range then the parameter being tuned will be set to the initial value multiplied by :ref:`TUNE_RANGE<TUNE_RANGE>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:108
#: 7e066e03cd594dca83d7dc4ab3280241
msgid "So with a default value for :ref:`TUNE_RANGE<TUNE_RANGE>` of 2 you will be able to change the parameter in a range from half its initial value to 2x the initial value. This is a good range for many tuning tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:113
#: dbcad60fcbde4baf959cb4fc5f566ef7
msgid "Activating the tuning knob"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:115
#: aca6fc961118423dafff3fabe5fc0b5c
msgid "When you first start tuning a parameter you will find the tuning knob is not yet active. This is because the knob does not activate until it passes the \"mid-point value\", defined as half way between :ref:`TUNE_CHAN_MIN<TUNE_CHAN_MIN>` and :ref:`TUNE_CHAN_MAX<TUNE_CHAN_MAX>`. Activating the tuning knob in this way ensures that you don't accidentally take off with a large change in tuning value. You are guaranteed to start the tune with a value very close to your current value for the parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:123
#: 583e928e515346f696000164a8b226d5
msgid "When the tuning knob activates by reaching the mid-point the buzzer on the flight board will give a quick \"bup-bip\" sound to indicate that tuning has been activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:128
#: 1a884ad930cf4aff90811063f6258590
msgid "Re-centering the tuning knob"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:130
#: e7ba1a36e4204701b8f90e0184699070
msgid "It is quite common to find that the :ref:`TUNE_RANGE<TUNE_RANGE>` is not wide enough to move the tuning value to the ideal point for your vehicle. For example, you may have started the tune with a P gain for some axis of 0.7, and when you move the tuning knob up all the way the vehicle still hasn't started oscillating. In that case the tuning value will have reached 1.4 and you need some more range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:137
#: 710b6130e9b14051809f8a6fcd85eb30
msgid "To get more range you can use the selector switch to re-center the tuning knob around the current value. Toggle the selector switch briefly high then low and the center-value will change to whatever the tubing knob is set to. When you re-center the tuning knob will de-activate again until you move it to the mid-point position. This prevents you from getting a jump in the tuning value when you re-center."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:145
#: a3bccc0c39374de6964439579a5d4ed9
msgid "Tuning multiple parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:147
#: e0d1d7aa30b74c3faac609d12bfcc00b
msgid "You can tune multiple parameters in one flight by setting :ref:`TUNE_PARAM<TUNE_PARAM>` to one of the \"tuning set\" parameters. For example, if you set :ref:`TUNE_PARAM<TUNE_PARAM>` to 101 then you will have 4 different stages to your tune:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:151
#: ad6e54eb28e641588c08e3674be1c54d
msgid "``Roll: Rate D``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:152
#: 78f6ecae14e045a09a74a75873dbb5c0
msgid "``Roll: Rate P and Rate I``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:153
#: cb3cefb3e9434593839e8440a192cd93
msgid "``Pitch: Rate D``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:154
#: a54272c2dfa04254bfaf58b0e4a56101
msgid "``Pitch: Rate P and Rate I``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:156
#: d340ba7950784ce1823ab233ded379c7
msgid "notice that ``Roll: Rate P and Rate I`` is actually two parameters in one, controlling both the P gain and the I gain for roll. This follows the normal advice for MultiCopters that you should keep the P and I values equal when doing a manual tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:161
#: f6feffd714a24de29cfffba1db58883a
msgid "When you choose a tuning set with :ref:`TUNE_PARAM<TUNE_PARAM>` then you will initially be tuning the first parameter in the set. Once you have adjusted that parameter as much as you need to you can move to the next parameter in the set by holding the selector switch for more than 2 seconds. It is suggested that you count to 3 to ensure you are over 2 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:167
#: 5f75c233eb814a3eba26c3a54bd3864f
msgid "Holding the selector switch for more than 2 seconds will switch you to the next parameter and will also change the tuning knob back to its \"wait for mid-point\" state on the new parameter. The buzzer on the board will give a loud BEEP sequence to indicate which parameter in the set you have changed to. For the first parameter in the set, you will get one loud BEEP. For the second parameter, you will get two loud BEEPs and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-transmitter-tuning.rst:175
#: c410143720ef4655a36ce7db0e2ac8a7
msgid "When you have cycled through all of the parameters in the tuning set you have chosen it will wrap back around to the first parameter in the set."
msgstr ""

